Functional Requirements
1. Daily File Processing

The system shall:

Download Active Employee CSV from S3.
Download Inactive Employee CSV from S3.
Load files into staging tables.
Validate files before updating production data.
2. Data Validation

The system must validate:

Duplicate Employees

No duplicate GLOBAL_ID should exist within a file.

Active/Inactive Conflict

An employee cannot exist in both Active and Inactive files in the same batch.

Mandatory Fields

Required fields:

Plain Text
GLOBAL_ID
EmployeeCode
OFFICIAL_EMAIL
Record Count Validation

The system should detect abnormal headcount drops or spikes before applying updates.

Example:

Plain Text
Previous Active Count: 10000
Current Active Count: 9950

Valid.

Plain Text
Previous Active Count: 10000
Current Active Count: 1200

Potentially invalid.

3. Employee Synchronization
New Employees

If a GLOBAL_ID exists in Active CSV but not in All_GeoEmpDataDEX_WV:

Plain Text
Insert Employee
Existing Employees

If employee exists and any attributes have changed:

Plain Text
Update Employee

Examples:

Manager Changes
Department Changes
Country Changes
Email Changes
Designation Changes
Separated Employees

If employee exists in Inactive CSV:

Plain Text
Mark employee as separated/inactive

Do not physically delete the record.

Reactivated Employees

If an employee was previously marked inactive but appears again in Active CSV:

Plain Text
Reactivate employee
